Yes — **early Buddhism is probably an even cleaner second vertical than late Platonism**, especially if the center is not “translate the Pāli canon” but:

> **map competing interpretations of the early discourses passage-by-passage, with Ñāṇananda and Ñāṇavīra as major interpretive lenses.**

That is extremely compatible with what you just built.

SuttaCentral/Bilara already handles the thing you should *not* rebuild: segmented root texts, translations, stable segment alignment and machine-readable corpus infrastructure. Your opportunity is the layer above that: **why does this passage mean what a translator/commentator claims it means?** Ñāṇavīra explicitly built *Notes on Dhamma* around correcting what he saw as misreadings of the Pāli suttas, and his site stresses that the Notes presuppose engagement with the original Pāli. ([Path Press Publications][1])

That makes the Pāṭala audit model almost perfect.

